Subject: [PATCH 08018/11362] [outer-loop] Correction: I cited exp6012 as
 showing "the gate is fine" when its own docstring says the opposite

Commit 24c2d51e4 claimed, as point 6 of the bottleneck chain, that "the gate is not
broken -- in the same matrix a correct hand-written `base` engine is admitted 31/33 and
`identity` 0/33, it discriminates exactly as designed."

That was wrong, and the artifact I cited says so in as many words.

In 30 of those 33 rows `base` is not a hand-written rule at all -- it is `visible_lookup`,
a table tabulated from the corpus. exp6012's docstring designates it an ATTACK BASELINE
and explicitly "never the must-not-fire control", because these are HIDDEN-STATE games:
the same visible grid under the same action has different successors depending on state
the grid does not show, so any table keyed on what is visible must be wrong on the
collisions. That file even records having made the inverse mistake itself once (it
originally called the table `corpus_oracle` and asserted it perfect by construction).

The genuine must-not-fire control is dc22's hand-written general rule, and there the
measured result is the OPPOSITE of what I claimed: REQ-6011 admits it 3/3, but the LIVE
hidden-state gate REJECTS it on 2/3. exp6012's own summary is that this gate is
"simultaneously too STRICT on an honest partial model and BLIND to a spurious writer" --
hence its verdict `complete_hidden_state_gate_hole_measured_req6011_not_wired_into_that_
branch`. Far from being fine, the gate has a measured hole.

WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT CHANGE. The headline is unaffected, because it never rested
on the comparator: the induced engines' changed-cell recall (median 0.0033, max 0.0870
over 11 games x 3 seeds) is a direct property of those engines, computed from exp6012's
recorded correct/true changed-cell counts, and no admission threshold from 0.90 down to
0.10 admits any of them. What changes is the INFERENCE I drew from it. I am no longer
entitled to say "the gate is correct to reject them"; I am entitled to say that at ~0.3%
changed-cell recall they are not honest partial models being unfairly excluded, so ANY
correctly calibrated gate rejects them, and fixing the gate hole -- worth doing on its own
merits -- will not move banked levels while induction is where it is.

The only part of the original point 6 that survives is the `identity` rejection (0/33).

Both the research note and the verifier-gap entry are corrected in place with the
correction stated rather than silently rewritten, per never-prune.

